# SEO parity standards

These patterns were established to bring AFL closer to the highest-performing sister site (Astra). Follow them for all new calculators and pages.

## Structured data (root layout)

Root `src/app/layout.tsx` renders:
- **OrganizationJsonLd** — site identity
- **SoftwareApplicationJsonLd** — with `featureList` (12 calculators) and `aggregateRating` (4.8/95)

Both are defined in `src/components/seo/JsonLd.tsx`.

Homepage (`src/app/[locale]/page.tsx`) emits:
- **WebSite** with `SearchAction`
- **ItemList** listing all live tools

## FAQSection emits JSON-LD

`FAQSection` in `src/components/calculators/ResultsSection.tsx` automatically emits **FAQPage** JSON-LD alongside visible FAQ content. Every calculator that passes FAQ items gets rich results. Do NOT create a visible FAQ without the JSON-LD — they are now coupled.

## Calculator page requirements

Every calculator using `CalculatorShell` must have:
1. Server-rendered educational intro (not hidden behind interaction)
2. FAQ items (rendered via `FAQSection` with auto JSON-LD)
3. Related tools links
4. Breadcrumb + WebApplication JSON-LD (auto from CalculatorShell)

For new calculators, add i18n copy in `messages/en/tools.json` — do NOT hardcode English strings in the page component.

## Zodiac-love static profiles

`zodiac-love/page.tsx` renders all 12 sign profiles as static `<article>` elements with anchor IDs, always visible to crawlers. The interactive selector is kept for UX but is NOT the only way to access content.

Pattern: interactive features enhance server-rendered content, they don't gate it.

## Editorial guide pages

`src/app/[locale]/guides/[slug]/page.tsx` serves articles from `src/lib/editorial-content.ts`. Each article has:
- 600-1000 words of genuine astrological educational content
- 3-5 sections with H2 headings
- FAQPage + BreadcrumbList + Article JSON-LD
- Links to 2-3 related calculators
- Navigation to other guides

Hub page at `/guides` lists all articles. When `relatedEditorial` slugs are added to `tool-registry.ts`, create matching content in `editorial-content.ts`.

## i18n publication

`src/i18n/locales.ts` controls publication status. Currently published: **en, es, pt**.

Before publishing a new locale:
1. Verify `messages/{locale}/tools.json` has full translations (not empty `{}`)
2. Verify `messages/{locale}/common.json` matches EN key count
3. Add translated routes in `src/i18n/translated-routes.ts`

The sitemap automatically picks up published locales and generates hreflang.

## Sign-pair programmatic pages

78 pair pages at `/compatibility/[pair]` are AFL's strongest programmatic SEO asset. Content in `src/lib/sign-pairs.ts` (`PAIR_INSIGHTS`). Each pair page has unique scores, strengths/challenges, element analysis, and FAQ.

## Security headers & consent

`next.config.ts` sets full CSP, security headers, and `poweredByHeader: false`. `ConsentBanner` component handles GDPR consent with localStorage key `afl.analytics-consent`.

## googleBot directives

Root metadata includes `googleBot` with `max-image-preview: "large"` and `max-snippet: -1`. Do not weaken these.

## Custom 404

Branded not-found page at `src/app/not-found.tsx`. Maintain the design when modifying.
